# Check every text file out with LF endings, on every platform.
#
# Without this, git on Windows converts to CRLF on checkout (core.autocrlf),
# while .prettierrc requires `endOfLine: "lf"`. The two fight forever: prettier
# --check fails, `prettier --write` fixes it, and the next checkout undoes the
# fix. Anything running that check gets stuck in a loop with no cause visible
# in the code.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binary files and leave them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
